 The user has paused the benchmark sweep while additional patches and workstreams arrive. Continue repair builds and correctness checks; do not start a benchmark sweep.
 
-When benchmarking resumes, use one repetition initially. Measure the upstream baseline and final eCash and V2 endpoints first. Within each layer, enqueue the midpoint of its unmeasured interval, then process the left and right subintervals breadth first. Continue until every eligible patch boundary is measured. Pre-register the schedule against an immutable canonical manifest; record unavailable metrics and grouped prerequisites explicitly.
+When benchmarking resumes, use one repetition initially. Measure four anchors first: upstream baseline, final eCash, the first operational native-consensus boundary, and final V2. Identify the consensus boundary by stable contract ID, not a renumbered ordinal. Within each layer, enqueue the midpoint of its unmeasured interval, then process the left and right subintervals breadth first. Continue until every eligible patch boundary is measured. Pre-register the schedule against an immutable canonical manifest; record unavailable metrics and grouped prerequisites explicitly.
 
 This is a coverage schedule, not a monotonicity-based regression bisect: performance may rise and fall repeatedly. Do not discard intervals because their endpoints match. If an early interval shows a large change, it can be prioritized while retaining all remaining work.
 
@@ -15,11 +15,35 @@ Endpoint comparisons are preliminary single-run observations. They do not attrib
 `daemon/scripts/schedule-patch-benchmarks.py` generates the schedule deterministically from the canonical manifest. By default it only previews/saves a plan:
 
 ```sh
-python3 daemon/scripts/schedule-patch-benchmarks.py --plan /path/to/schedule.json
+python3 daemon/scripts/schedule-patch-benchmarks.py --consensus-owner 112 --plan /path/to/schedule.json
 ```
 
-When the sweep is explicitly resumed, add `--execute --data <results> --source <dedicated-replay-checkout> --build <incremental-build>` to that command. The source directory is a disposable benchmark clone, not the consolidated development checkout. `--limit 3` visits just the three endpoint points. Omit the limit to fill every point in the schedule. Defaults are one repetition and two build jobs.
+When the sweep is explicitly resumed, add `--execute --data <results> --source <dedicated-replay-checkout> --build <incremental-build>` to that command. The source directory is a disposable benchmark clone, not the consolidated development checkout. `--limit 4` visits the four anchors when `--consensus-owner` is supplied. Owner `112` currently introduces native consensus connection; its runtime workload still needs validation at that exact boundary. Omit the limit to fill every point in the schedule. Defaults are one repetition and two build jobs.
 
 Each point invokes `patch-progression.py --point N`. It replays the exact patch prefix, verifies every intermediate canonical tree, then builds, tests and benchmarks only N. Earlier unmeasured points receive no fabricated test/benchmark successes. Matching results are reused by the runner's prefix/harness/source-tree checks; the first failure stops the scheduler and writes its normal failure packet. Re-running the same command resumes through those identity checks. A changed candidate or runner requires a new schedule file. This scheduler never invokes an LLM.
 
 Verification includes complete unique coverage across uneven/empty layer intervals, endpoint-first breadth order, stop-on-failure, changed-candidate rejection, and a real two-patch Git replay without preceding results. The replay test deliberately fails configuration to verify the failure packet and sparse resume command; it does not run daemon benchmarks. Full daemon execution against the final repaired stack remains pending, and the sweep remains held.
+
+
+## Pinned build profiles and current readiness
+
+`--cmake-flags-file /path/to/profile.json` accepts a complete JSON array of
+`-DNAME=value` definitions. The scheduler pins its contents and hash, and the
+runner includes it in result identity and failure-resume commands. Use separate
+result directories for different profiles. Explicit profiles replace the historical
+wallet-OFF/Chronik-OFF defaults. Chronik validation builds obey `--jobs`; no
+additional eight-job compiler cohort is launched.
+
+The historical Layer1 and Layer2 stress scripts are separate frozen sources, not
+one automatically adaptive script. Their recorded files match ecash-tip and
+`09f95c297a` respectively. The native script's version2-negative check spends a
+native coin: preserve that rejection after the legacy bridge, but update its obsolete
+`bad-txns-non-v7-format` expectation to the specified typed-spend rejection. Native
+output encoding, RPC amounts, and signing fixtures must be checked against the
+current implementation before measuring. A header-only native prefix with no
+applicable workload must be reported unavailable, never as a zero-throughput
+measurement or a successful end-to-end benchmark.
+
+Planning and harness regression tests do not authorize execution or establish
+node correctness. Wait for root candidate promotion/preflight and a resource
+coordinator grant before starting any compiler or daemon benchmark cohort.
